# Repository Knowledge Map

This map explains every Reporivet-installed path and routes Agents to project-owned authority. The default onboarding entry point is integrated `reporivet setup`; `reporivet init` remains structure-only, and the lower-level `reporivet define` flow remains available. Reporivet installs documents and fixed Claude adapters; it does not install a repository-local executor, CI, completion engine, evidence archive, deployment engine, or task database.

## Reading protocol

1. Read root [`AGENTS.md`](../AGENTS.md).
2. For substantive work, create or resume one matching Plan in [`exec-plans/active/`](exec-plans/active/).
3. Follow the Plan's exact reads, boundaries, acceptance criteria, and current checkpoint.
4. Read only the relevant authority below and use project-owned commands from [`QUALITY.md`](QUALITY.md) or [`OPERATIONS.md`](OPERATIONS.md).

## Canonical paths

| Path | Purpose and ownership |
|---|---|
| `.gitignore` | Reporivet owns only its marked block, which ignores machine-local `.claude/settings.local.json`; surrounding project rules are preserved. |
| `AGENTS.md` | Canonical host-neutral Agent operating contract. Reporivet owns only its marked block and preserves surrounding project text. |
| `CLAUDE.md` | Claude Code adapter, created only when missing; the default content is exactly `@AGENTS.md`. Existing content is preserved. |
| `.claude/skills/reporivet-main/SKILL.md` | Instruction-only Main procedure, created only when missing. |
| `.claude/skills/reporivet-implementation/SKILL.md` | Instruction-only bounded implementation procedure, created only when missing. |
| `.claude/skills/reporivet-verification/SKILL.md` | Instruction-only fresh-context verification procedure, created only when missing. |
| `.claude/skills/<slug>/SKILL.md` | Optional project-owned instruction-only procedure Skill, created only by resumed setup from a complete Confirmed structured procedure record; no project-specific Skill is pre-generated. |
| `.claude/settings.json` | Optional shared Claude Code settings. Absent by default; a reviewed deny-only file can be created only after exact preview approval and is never merged or rewritten. It is defense in depth, not a sandbox. |
| `.claude/settings.local.json` | User/machine-local Claude settings; referenced by the ignore block but never generated, read, or managed. |
| `.reporivet-version` | Small create-if-missing package ownership/version marker. |
